dropped the body of function
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/1-3, [dcl.fct]/12: the declaration `ostream<char>
*set_rdbuf(streambuf *)' in ios<char> does not require ostream<char> to
be complete.  typecheck_compound_body exempted member function
declarations from instantiating the classes they name, but tested for a
declarator of type ID_code, which an unconverted member function
declarator never is (it is a function_type): ostream<char> was
instantiated within ios<char> and missed its member set_rdbuf, and
ofstream's constructor was dropped ("member ... set_rdbuf ... not
found").  bin53 passes this test (the regression came with the
[temp.inst]/1 exemption added since).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
